{"chunk_id":"003181","wall_time_seconds":0.888756228,"exit_code":0,"original_token_count":3730,"output":"## Task 3: Implement and deploy native Typst editing, proof, PDF, and persistence

### rollout_summary_files

- rollout_summaries/2026-09-26T11-02-50-0rjp-twyne_native_typst_editor_implementation_deployment.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/26/rollout-2026-09-26T07-02-50-01a0dd61-d08c-7f71-9e6c-24cf8966c3df.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-29T01:38:36+00:00, thread_id=01a0dd61-d08c-7f71-9e6c-24cf8966c3df, success; CI, Railway, and live proof/PDF/persistence smoke passed)

### keywords

- Typst, @myriaddreamin/typst.ts, CodeMirror, ProseMirror, typst-workspace, typst-code-editor, format, typstSource, compiler.worker.ts, mammoth.browser, import.meta.glob, Convex, Railway

## User preferences

- when narration is invoked from a character’s “lecteur,” the user wanted the player to know “what character was being called” -> resolve and display that persona’s voice by default, never a generic voice when identity is known. [Task 1]
- when requesting “full dubplex voice” that can “edit and add information searach and interact with the app,” and premium/credit use -> show captions, action state, consent, wallet/cost ceilings, and require approval before manuscript mutation. [Task 2]
- when starting the Typst plan, the user said “focus on implementation” and “focus on implementation not test” -> ship the functional slice before expanding tests, while retaining the visual/page editor as an opt-in Typst source workflow rather than replacing it. [Task 3]

## Reusable knowledge

- `src/utils/speech.ts` owns the shared narration queue/player; persona identity flows through `author`, `label`, `voice`, and provider-specific `voices`. `src/utils/personas.ts` holds display names, IDs, roles, voice overrides, and direction. Do not pass generic OpenAI voice names directly to Supertonic/browser narration; map them to supported embeddings or persona overrides. [Task 1]
- Twyne’s Live client uses Not Organic `/v1/live/sessions` through same-origin `/api/live`; provider billing/entitlements remain authoritative and Twyne never receives an OpenAI key. The implementation reserves ceilings of `$0.50` per session and `$0.05` per delegated action, not quoted rates. [Task 2]
- Draft edits are proposals first: later spoken/UI approval checks manuscript revision, rejects ambiguous repeated passages, preserves rich text, remains undoable, and stops when the workspace/folio changes. Only provider-returned research results may be described as web results; local placeholders are rejected. [Task 2]
- The provider patch adds a one-time `$2.50` Twyne welcome allowance separate from Keating, with idempotency and paid-history exclusions. Delegated replies are accepted only for IDs observed from trusted upstream events; inspect the separate provider dirty tree before follow-up work. [Task 2]
- Native Typst documents use `@myriaddreamin/typst.ts` in a client worker with bundled fonts/assets, CodeMirror source editing, proof-page rendering, downloadable source, and PDF export; source edits compile without a server round trip. `format` and `typstSource` persistence/sync fields retain HTML projection compatibility for legacy documents and integrations. [Task 3]
- Core paths are `src/utils/typst/{document,serialize,export,client,session,compiler.worker}.ts`, `src/components/editor/{typst-workspace,typst-code-editor}.tsx`, `src/components/editor/extensions/raw-typst.ts`, `src/utils/{idb,convex-sync}.ts`, `convex/schema.ts`, and `convex/sync.ts`. Production smoke at `https://twyne.love/editor/` rendered two proof pages, produced a `%PDF-` download, preserved content on reload, and showed no runtime errors. [Task 3]

## Failures and how to do differently

- Feature checks do not establish real microphone permissions, visual UI, deployed WebSocket behavior, provider availability/credit debit, or production consent. Full typecheck initially exposed unrelated language/i18n errors; report targeted validation separately. [Task 2]
- A browser-only exporter leaked through shared serialization (`mammoth/mammoth.browser`) and failed Convex typecheck -> keep shared escaping in `src/utils/typst/string.ts` and keep backend imports browser-independent. Guard `import.meta.glob` tests with `const supportsViteModules = typeof import.meta.glob === "function"`; Bun does not provide it. [Task 3]
- Direct browser-global assignment/restoration caused 105 Bun failures -> save/restore descriptors with `Object.defineProperty`. Before push run `bun run lint`, `bun run fmt.check`, Convex typecheck, and the full suite; final validation was `1605 pass`, `40 skip`, `0 fail`, GitHub run `36508550529` success, and Railway deployment `2261ee43-1626-496b-8388-5e0c2d749989` successful. `bun add` can need `BUN_TMPDIR=/tmp BUN_INSTALL_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/twyne-bun-cache`. [Task 3]

